#
# We do NOT vendor the binary in the repository (it is a large, per-platform Go binary): it is
# staged into the Orodruin image and pinned. The adapter (annatar/engines/stratus.py) reads the
# staged binary and checks its sha256 against the `stratus` line below BEFORE EVERY phase (not
# only once per run; SEC5, like annatar/atomics/PIN) — a binary that is not the pinned one, or
# one swapped mid-run, runs nothing.
# `annatar run` never fetches Stratus; Orodruin has no Internet egress.
#
# ── The binary the adapter execs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sha256 of the `stratus` binary extracted from stratus-red-team_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz v2.38.0.
# This is the value checked at run time (BINARY_LABEL = "stratus").
#   376ceff19c170194f6adbc2f883e8b5658e99a13cb1057f0ab118524411d57bb  stratus
#
# ── Provenance (verified against the release's published checksums.txt) ─────────────────
# The upstream archive the binary is extracted from — its sha256 is the one DataDog publishes
# in the v2.38.0 `checksums.txt` asset. Recorded so the staging step can verify the download
# before extraction; the adapter checks the extracted binary above, which is what it execs.
#   2f0a971c7d8f5fb32a598f70b79c954d7aee72740d352947a78d348b00fb09a3  stratus-red-team_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz
#
# ── Embedded warmup assets (Orodruin has no Internet) ───────────────────────────────────
# Stratus's `warmup` provisions a technique's prerequisites with Terraform. Left to itself it
# would download, on first run, the Terraform binary and the azurerm/azuread provider plugins
# (docs/design/orodruin-contract.md forbids that egress). Both are staged into the image and
# the adapter points Stratus at them offline (annatar/engines/stratus.py::airgap_env):
#   - Terraform (the exact version Stratus auto-installs, pkg/stratus/runner/terraform.go:
#     TerraformVersion = "1.3.10"), pre-installed under the run-scoped HOME so Stratus finds it
#     and never downloads one. sha256 of the upstream zip (releases.hashicorp.com):
#       2e3931c3db6999cdd4c7e55227cb877c6946d1f52923d7d057036d2827311402  terraform_1.3.10_linux_amd64.zip
#   - the azurerm / azuread provider plugins each technique's lockfile pins, staged into a
#     filesystem mirror (TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE) + plugin cache (TF_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR) so
#     `terraform init` installs from disk, never the registry. Their sha256 are the ones in
#     each technique's `.terraform.lock.hcl`, recorded by the staging step (make stratus-stage,
#     annatar/stratus/README.md) — not invented here.
#
# To update Stratus: bump the version + date above, re-read the new release's checksums.txt,
# replace the `stratus` and archive sha256, re-stage the assets, and run the harness (ID1).
